{
 "cells": [
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "# gl(3), L = 1: the 3x3 SoV scalar-product determinant with abstract Q\n\nCompanion to `SU3_Adjoint_SoV_ScalarProduct_L2.wb` and `SU3_Adjoint_Twisted_SoV_L2.wb`, but **formal**: no spin chain is built, no eigenvalue problem is solved. The direct functions `Q_i` and the dual functions `Q^j` are undetermined symbols. Everything below is exact rational algebra in `theta`, `h` and the Q-values at a handful of lattice points.\n\n## Setup\n\nOne site, rep `lambda = {2,1,0}` (adjoint), inhomogeneity `theta`, shift `h`.\n\n$$\\nu_i(u) = u-\\theta-h\\lambda_i,\\qquad \\nu_1 = u-\\theta-2h,\\ \\nu_2 = u-\\theta-h,\\ \\nu_3 = u-\\theta .$$\n\n$$\\mu(u) = \\frac{1}{(u-\\theta)(u-\\theta-h)},\\qquad M(u) \\;=\\; \\frac{\\mu}{\\nu_1} \\;=\\; \\frac{1}{\\nu_1\\nu_2\\nu_3},$$\n\nso `M` has the **three** simple poles `theta, theta+h, theta+2h`.\n\n## Why three columns\n\nWith the (unimodular) twist on, `T_1 = chi_1 u + c_1` and `T_2 = chi_2 u^2 + s_2 u + c_2`; the leading coefficients `chi_1 = sum z_i`, `chi_2 = sum_{i<j} z_i z_j` are state-independent. Hence\n\n$$\\Delta T_1 = \\Delta c_1 \\ (\\deg 0),\\qquad \\Delta T_2 = \\Delta s_2\\,u + \\Delta c_2 \\ (\\deg 1),$$\n\nthree non-trivial integrals of motion. The L=2 identity\n\n$$0 \\;=\\; \\big\\langle -\\Delta T_1\\, Q^j Q_i \\;+\\; \\delta_1\\, Q^j Q_i^{[-2]} \\;+\\; \\delta_2^{[2]}\\, Q^{j[2]} Q_i \\big\\rangle_M,\\qquad \\Delta T_2 = \\nu_1^{[-2]}\\delta_1 + \\nu_3\\,\\delta_2,$$\n\nhas, at L=1, **constant** `delta_1 = a_1`, `delta_2 = a_2` (both `nu_1^{[-2]}` and `nu_3` are linear and share no root, `3h != 0`). So the six L=2 columns collapse to three:\n\n$$G_1 = -Q^j Q_i,\\qquad G_2 = Q^j Q_i^{[-2]},\\qquad G_3 = Q^{j[2]} Q_i,$$\n\npaired with `w' = (Delta c_1, a_1, a_2)`. Rows are labelled by a direct index `i` and a dual index `j`.\n\n## Target\n\nExpand the 3x3 determinant by residues and express it through the SoV wave function\n\n$$\\Psi(\\{x_{21}\\},\\{x_{11},x_{22}\\}) \\;=\\; Q_1(x_{21})\\,\\big[\\,Q_1(x_{11})Q_2(x_{22}-h) - Q_2(x_{11})Q_1(x_{22}-h)\\,\\big].$$",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* ---- 1. L=1 kinematics: the nu's, the quantum determinant, the measure M and its three simple poles. ---- *)\nClearAll[lam, nu, nu1, nu2, nu3, qdet, muMeas, Mmeas, E2meas, poles, resw, bracketM, u, h, th, x];\nlam = {2, 1, 0};\nnu[i_][y_] := y - th - h lam[[i]];\nnu1[y_] := nu[1][y];\nnu2[y_] := nu[2][y];\nnu3[y_] := nu[3][y];\nqdet[y_] := nu1[y - 2 h] nu2[y - h] nu3[y];\nmuMeas[y_] := 1/((y - th) (y - th - h));\nMmeas[y_] := 1/(nu1[y] nu2[y] nu3[y]);\nE2meas[y_] := muMeas[y]/(nu1[y] nu1[y - h]);\npoles = th + h Range[0, 2];\nresw = Table[Together[Residue[Mmeas[x], {x, p}]], {p, poles}];\n(* full-contour functional: sum of residues of M(u) F(u) over the three poles *)\nbracketM[F_] := resw . Map[F, poles];\nGrid[{\n  {\"nu_1, nu_2, nu_3\", Table[nu[i][u], {i, 3}]},\n  {\"qdet = nu_1^[-4] nu_2^[-2] nu_3 (deg 3 = 3L)\", Expand[qdet[u]]},\n  {\"M = mu/nu_1\", Simplify[Mmeas[u] - muMeas[u]/nu1[u]] === 0},\n  {\"E_2 = mu/(nu_1 nu_1^[-2]) has 4 poles, M has 3\", {Denominator[Together[E2meas[u]]], Denominator[Together[Mmeas[u]]]}},\n  {\"poles of M\", poles},\n  {\"residue weights\", resw},\n  {\"weights = 1/prod_{p'!=p}(p-p')\", resw === Table[Together[1/Times @@ (p - DeleteCases[poles, p])], {p, poles}]},\n  {\"sum of weights vanishes (M ~ u^-3)\", Together[Total[resw]]}\n  }, Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
       "data": "<div class=\"wl-output-block\"><div class=\"wl-output-header\" style=\"display:flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;width:100%;min-height:22px;\" data-session-epoch=\"639557\" data-output-id=\"7\" data-out-n=\"14\" data-sub-idx=\"15\" data-output-format=\"WLLatex\" data-output-is-graphics=\"0\" data-cell-idx=\"1\" data-sub-start=\"15\" data-sub-end=\"24\"><span style=\"font-size:10px;color:#888;margin-right:8px;\">Out[14]=</span></div><div class=\"wl-output-content\"><div class=\"vscode-wolfram-wllatex-prerendered\" data-page-width-em=\"33\" data-latex-b64=\"\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:9.7084em;vertical-align:-4.5842em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:5.1242em;\"><span style=\"top:-7.0842em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:7.0842em;\"></span><span class=\"mtable\"><span class=\"vertical-separator\" style=\"height:9.6684em;border-right-width:0.04em;border-right-style:solid;margin:0 -0.02em;vertical-align:-4.5842em;\"></span><span class=\"arraycolsep\" style=\"width:0.5em;\"></span><span class=\"col-align-c\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:5.0842em;\"><span style=\"top:-7.2442em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">nu_1, nu_2, nu_3</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-5.9858em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">qdet = nu_1</span><span class=\"mord accent\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.6944em;\"><span style=\"top:-3em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-3em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"accent-body\" style=\"left:-0.25em;\"><span class=\"mord\">ˆ</span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord\">[-4] nu_2</span><span class=\"mord accent\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.6944em;\"><span style=\"top:-3em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-3em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"accent-body\" style=\"left:-0.25em;\"><span class=\"mord\">ˆ</span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord\">[-2] nu_3 (deg 3 = 3L)</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-4.7858em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">M = mu/nu_1</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.5858em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">E_2 = mu/(nu_1 nu_1</span><span class=\"mord accent\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.6944em;\"><span style=\"top:-3em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-3em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"accent-body\" style=\"left:-0.25em;\"><span class=\"mord\">ˆ</span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord\">[-2]) has 4 poles, M has 3</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-2.3858em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">poles of M</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-1.1758em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">residue weights</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:0.0242em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">weights = 1/prod_{p’!=p}(p-p’)</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:1.2242em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">sum of weights vanishes (M ~</span><span class=\"mord\"></span><span class=\"mord\"> u</span><span class=\"mord accent\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.6944em;\"><span style=\"top:-3em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-3em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"accent-body\" style=\"left:-0.25em;\"><span class=\"mord\">ˆ</span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord\">-3)</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:4.5842em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"arraycolsep\" style=\"width:0.5em;\"></span><span class=\"vertical-separator\" style=\"height:9.6684em;border-right-width:0.04em;border-right-style:solid;margin:0 -0.02em;vertical-align:-4.5842em;\"></span><span class=\"arraycolsep\" style=\"width:0.5em;\"></span><span class=\"col-align-c\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:5.0842em;\"><span style=\"top:-7.2442em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"minner\"><span class=\"mopen delimcenter\" style=\"top:0em;\">{</span><span class=\"mord\">−</span><span class=\"mord\">2</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">h</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">−</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></