=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">th</span></span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">2</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">h</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">th</span></span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">3</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">h</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">th</span></span><span class=\"mclose delimcenter\" style=\"top:0em;\">}</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-1.7899em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">True</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-0.5899em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">True</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:2.7701em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"arraycolsep\" style=\"width:0.5em;\"></span><span class=\"vertical-separator\" style=\"height:6.0401em;border-right-width:0.04em;border-right-style:solid;margin:0 -0.02em;vertical-align:-2.7701em;\"></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-2.5em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:5.2701em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.7em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:5.2701em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-4.9em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:5.2701em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-6.1em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:5.2701em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-7.3em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:5.2701em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-8.5401em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:5.2701em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:2.7701em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></div></div></div>",
       "mime": "x-application/wolfram-language-html"
      },
      {
       "data": "Out[31]= \\begin{array}{|c|c|}\\hline\\text{split of a generic linear DeltaT2 = ds2 u + dc2} & \\left\\{-\\frac{dc2+ds2\\,\\mathrm{th}}{3\\,h},\\frac{dc2+3\\,ds2\\,h+ds2\\,\\mathrm{th}}{3\\,h}\\right\\}\\\\\\hline\\text{check: nu1\\^{}[-2] a1 + nu3 a2 reproduces it} & \\mathrm{True}\\\\\\hline\\text{E\\_2 poles (4)} & \\left\\{\\mathrm{th},h+\\mathrm{th},2\\,h+\\mathrm{th},3\\,h+\\mathrm{th}\\right\\}\\\\\\hline\\text{E\\_2 -> M rewriting, 16 test pairs, dT1 = 5/7, dT2 = (3/4)u - 2/9} & \\mathrm{True}\\\\\\hline\\text{same with symbolic dT1, dT2} & \\mathrm{True}\\\\\\hline\\end{array}",
       "mime": "text/plain"
      }
     ],
     "id": "1c942e3d-1e5a-448f-9eab-6c4e7fba090f"
    }
   ],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 3. Abstract Q, the rows, and the determinant\n\nWrite `qu[i,n] = Q_i(theta + n h)` and `qd[j,n] = Q^j(theta + n h)`. The residues sample the direct functions at `n = -1,0,1,2` and the duals at `n = 0,1,2,3`. With `m = (1/(2h^2), -1/h^2, 1/(2h^2))` the row for the pair `(i,j)` is\n\n$$R_{(i,j)} \\;=\\; \\sum_{n=0}^{2} m_n\\, g_{(i,j)}(n),\\qquad g_{(i,j)}(n) = \\big(-qd_{j,n}\\,qu_{i,n},\\; qd_{j,n}\\,qu_{i,n-1},\\; qd_{j,n+1}\\,qu_{i,n}\\big).$$\n\nBecause each row is a **sum of three vectors**, the determinant is multilinear in rows and expands into 27 terms,\n\n$$\\det N \\;=\\; \\sum_{n_1,n_2,n_3=0}^{2} m_{n_1}m_{n_2}m_{n_3}\\; \\det\\!\\big[g_{(i_1,j_1)}(n_1);\\, g_{(i_2,j_2)}(n_2);\\, g_{(i_3,j_3)}(n_3)\\big].$$\n\nThis is the form in which the wave functions should become visible: each `3x3` determinant of `g`'s is built from products of `2x2` Casoratian-type minors.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* ---- 3. Abstract Q-functions, the (i,j) rows, and the 27-term multilinear expansion of the 3x3 determinant. ---- *)\nClearAll[QU, QD, qu, qd, toIdx, gvec, rowM, detN, detNexp, allRows];\n(* lattice-value symbols: qu[i,n] = Q_i(theta + n h), qd[j,n] = Q^j(theta + n h) *)\ntoIdx = {QU[i_][th + n_. h] :> qu[i, n], QU[i_][th] :> qu[i, 0], QD[j_][th + n_. h] :> qd[j, n], QD[j_][th] :> qd[j, 0]};\ngvec[{i_, j_}, n_] := {-qd[j, n] qu[i, n], qd[j, n] qu[i, n - 1], qd[j, n + 1] qu[i, n]};\n(* row (i,j): the three column integrals, evaluated by residues *)\nrowM[{i_, j_}] := Expand[(bracketM /@ colFunsM[QD[j], QU[i]]) /. toIdx];\n(* multilinear-in-rows expansion: 27 terms *)\ndetNexp[tr_] := Expand[Sum[Times @@ resw[[{n1, n2, n3} + 1]] Det[{gvec[tr[[1]], n1], gvec[tr[[2]], n2], gvec[tr[[3]], n3]}], {n1, 0, 2}, {n2, 0, 2}, {n3, 0, 2}]];\ndetN[tr_] := Expand[Det[rowM /@ tr]];\nallRows = Tuples[Range[3], 2];\nGrid[{\n  {\"row (1,1) as a vector of lattice values\", MatrixForm[rowM[{1, 1}]]},\n  {\"direct sample points n\", Union[Cases[rowM /@ allRows, qu[_, n_] :> n, Infinity]]},\n  {\"dual sample points n\", Union[Cases[rowM /@ allRows, qd[_, n_] :> n, Infinity]]},\n  {\"det via Det[rows] == 27-term multilinear expansion, all 84 triples\", And @@ Table[detN[tr] === detNexp[tr], {tr, Subsets[allRows, {3}]}]}\n  }, Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
       "data": "<div class=\"wl-output-block\"><div class=\"wl-output-header\" style=\"display:flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;width:100%;min-height:22px;\" data-session-epoch=\"639557\" data-output-id=\"10\" data-out-n=\"39\" data-sub-idx=\"11\" data-output-format=\"WLLatex\" data-output-is-graphics=\"0\" data-cell-idx=\"5\" data-sub-start=\"11\" data-sub-end=\"16\"><span style=\"font-size:10px;color:#888;margin-right:8px;\">Out[39]=</span></div><div class=\"wl-output-content\"><div class=\"vscode-wolfram-wllatex-prerendered\" data-page-width-em=\"33\" data-latex-b64=\"\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:10.879em;vertical-align:-5.1695em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:5.7095em;\"><span style=\"top:-7.6695em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:7.6695em;\"></span><span class=\"mtable\"><span class=\"vertical-separator\" style=\"height:10.839em;border-right-width:0.04em;border-right-style:solid;margin:0 -0.02em;vertical-align:-5.1695em;\"></span><span class=\"arraycolsep\" style=\"width:0.5em;\"></span><span class=\"col-align-c\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:5.6695em;\"><span style=\"top:-7.6695em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:5.8695em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">row (1,1) as a vector of lattice values</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.46em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:5.8695em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">direct sample points n</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-2.26em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:5.8695em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">dual sample points n</span></span></span></sp