"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">2</span><span class=\"mclose delimcenter\" style=\"top:0em;\">}</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-2.26em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:5.8695em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"minner\"><span class=\"mopen delimcenter\" style=\"top:0em;\">{</span><span class=\"mord\">0</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">2</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">3</span><span class=\"mclose delimcenter\" style=\"top:0em;\">}</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-1.06em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:5.8695em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">True</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:5.1695em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"arraycolsep\" style=\"width:0.5em;\"></span><span class=\"vertical-separator\" style=\"height:10.839em;border-right-width:0.04em;border-right-style:solid;margin:0 -0.02em;vertical-align:-5.1695em;\"></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-2.5em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:7.6695em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.7em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:7.6695em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-4.9em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:7.6695em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-6.1em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:7.6695em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-13.339em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:7.6695em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:5.1695em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></div></div></div>",
       "mime": "x-application/wolfram-language-html"
      },
      {
       "data": "Out[39]= \\begin{array}{|c|c|}\\hline\\text{row (1,1) as a vector of lattice values} & \\left(\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{\\mathrm{qd}\\left(1,0\\right)\\,\\mathrm{qu}\\left(1,0\\right)}{2\\,h^2}+\\frac{\\mathrm{qd}\\left(1,1\\right)\\,\\mathrm{qu}\\left(1,1\\right)}{h^2}-\\frac{\\mathrm{qd}\\left(1,2\\right)\\,\\mathrm{qu}\\left(1,2\\right)}{2\\,h^2}\\\\\\frac{\\mathrm{qd}\\left(1,0\\right)\\,\\mathrm{qu}\\left(1,-1\\right)}{2\\,h^2}-\\frac{\\mathrm{qd}\\left(1,1\\right)\\,\\mathrm{qu}\\left(1,0\\right)}{h^2}+\\frac{\\mathrm{qd}\\left(1,2\\right)\\,\\mathrm{qu}\\left(1,1\\right)}{2\\,h^2}\\\\\\frac{\\mathrm{qd}\\left(1,1\\right)\\,\\mathrm{qu}\\left(1,0\\right)}{2\\,h^2}-\\frac{\\mathrm{qd}\\left(1,2\\right)\\,\\mathrm{qu}\\left(1,1\\right)}{h^2}+\\frac{\\mathrm{qd}\\left(1,3\\right)\\,\\mathrm{qu}\\left(1,2\\right)}{2\\,h^2}\\end{aligned}\\right)\\\\\\hline\\text{direct sample points n} & \\left\\{-1,0,1,2\\right\\}\\\\\\hline\\text{dual sample points n} & \\left\\{0,1,2,3\\right\\}\\\\\\hline\\text{det via Det[rows] == 27-term multilinear expansion, all 84 triples} & \\mathrm{True}\\\\\\hline\\end{array}",
       "mime": "text/plain"
      }
     ],
     "id": "d08a85f9-16f8-445e-a4ae-efb2a994047f"
    }
   ],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 4. The wave functions\n\nThe direct sample points are `n = -1,0,1,2` and the dual ones `n = 0,1,2,3`. That is exactly what the two wave functions produce if all three separated variables run over the three poles `n = 0,1,2`:\n\n$$\\Psi^B(x_{21};x_{11},x_{22}) \\;=\\; Q_1(x_{21})\\Big[Q_1(x_{11})Q_2(x_{22}-h) - Q_2(x_{11})Q_1(x_{22}-h)\\Big],$$\n\n$$\\Psi^A(x_{21};x_{11},x_{22}) \\;=\\; Q^1(x_{21})\\Big[Q^1(x_{11})Q^2(x_{22}+h) - Q^2(x_{11})Q^1(x_{22}+h)\\Big],$$\n\nthe dual one carrying the opposite shift. `Psi^B` reaches `n = -1` through `x_{22}-h`, `Psi^A` reaches `n = 3` through `x_{22}+h`; nothing else is sampled.\n\nBoth are cubic in the Q's, and so is `det N`, so the question\n\n$$\\det N \\;\\stackrel{?}{=}\\; \\sum_{x_{21},x_{11},x_{22}\\in\\{0,h,2h\\}} m(x)\\,\\Psi^A(x)\\,\\Psi^B(x)$$\n\nis an exact linear problem for the 27 weights `m(x)`. Only the four rows with `i,j` in `{1,2}` stay inside `Q_1,Q_2,Q^1,Q^2`, so there are four candidate triples.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* ---- 4. Exact linear solve for the weights m(x) in det N = Sum_x m(x) PsiA(x) PsiB(x). ---- *)\nClearAll[PsiB, PsiA, confs, wsym, fitPsi, fitTab, cand];\n(* separated variables carry integer labels n, meaning theta + n h *)\nPsiB[{x21_, x11_, x22_}] := qu[1, x21] (qu[1, x11] qu[2, x22 - 1] - qu[2, x11] qu[1, x22 - 1]);\nPsiA[{x21_, x11_, x22_}] := qd[1, x21] (qd[1, x11] qd[2, x22 + 1] - qd[2, x11] qd[1, x22 + 1]);\nconfs = Tuples[{0, 1, 2}, 3];\n(* exact coefficient matching: unknowns are the 27 weights *)\nfitPsi[tr_] := Module[{tgt, ans, vs, eqs, sol, ws},\n   ws = Array[wsym, Length[confs]];\n   tgt = detN[tr];\n   ans = Expand[Sum[ws[[c]] PsiA[confs[[c]]] PsiB[confs[[c]]], {c, Length[confs]}]];\n   vs = Union@Cases[{tgt, ans}, qu[_, _] | qd[_, _], Infinity];\n   eqs = Thread[Last /@ CoefficientRules[Expand[tgt - ans], vs] == 0];\n   sol = Solve[eqs, ws];\n   If[sol === {}, \"NO SOLUTION\", Thread[confs -> (ws /. First[sol])]]];\ncand = {{{1, 1}, {2, 1}, {2, 2}}, {{1, 1}, {1, 2}, {2, 1}}, {{1, 1}, {1, 2}, {2, 2}}, {{1, 2}, {2, 1}, {2, 2}}};\nfitTab = Table[tr -> fitPsi[tr], {tr, cand}];\nGrid[Prepend[Table[{fitTab[[k, 1]], If[StringQ[fitTab[[k, 2]]], fitTab[[k, 2]], \"solvable\"]}, {k, Length[cand]}], {\"triple (i,j)\", \"status\"}], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
